186566642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566922 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566922 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566922 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566922 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566922 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566922 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566922 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186566769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566922 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "663a5ef1-2806-5743-91be-acd7d7ce6565" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567031 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567031 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105657" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567031 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567031 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨y\\operatorname{ln}⁡z,z\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2},$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567031 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3654dbb4-b86f-5d3a-b4a5-c4e336a8010d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567031 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2x,4y,6z⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0+0+0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2y+3z)\\cdot 0+⟨y\\operatorname{ln}⁡z,z\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y⟩\\cdot ⟨2x,4y,6z⟩ \\\\  & =2xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+4yz\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+6xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567041 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567041 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105632" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567041 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567041 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F-G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2})\\,i-\\frac{1}{y}\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567041 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55481d4d-7e9b-585b-a201-3605d4c46b9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567041 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-G) & =∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot (-G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2}))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x{y}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-G) & =∇\\cdot F-∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567087 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567087 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105650" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567087 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567087 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\operatorname{sin}⁡y⟩$ and $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567087 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d754555e-e33d-5cf1-883c-d6ab614cfeb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567087 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\operatorname{sin}⁡y⟩\\cdot ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y⟩ \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡y-{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡y \\\\  & =({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)+({cos}^{2}⁡y-{sin}^{2}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567096 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567096 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567096 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567096 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F-5G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF=({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,i+xy\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=x-y.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567096 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e36ebfc7-87b5-5b58-93d4-2765b6334842" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567096 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-5G) & =∇\\cdot F-∇\\cdot (5G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-5∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy) \\\\  & =2x+x \\\\  & =3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-5G) & =∇\\cdot F-5∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =3x-5\\cdot (x-y) \\\\  & =3x-5x+5y \\\\  & =5y-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
